\section{PDE Closure Benchmark \& Model Discovery}
% ==============================================================================

Empirically discovered PDE closures are evaluated against standard neutral momentum formulations using a 12-mode Gegenbauer Spectral Galerkin expansion integrated with the stiff \texttt{Rodas5P} Rosenbrock solver.

\subsection{Why a Gegenbauer Basis?}

Gegenbauer polynomials $C_n^{(\lambda)}(x)$ form an orthogonal family on $[-1,1]$ under the weight $w_\lambda(x)=(1-x^2)^{\lambda-1/2}$. The benchmark uses the affine physical map
\begin{equation}
    z=\frac{H}{2}(x+1), \qquad H=100\,\mathrm{m},
\end{equation}
with $\lambda=0.75$, so $w_{0.75}(x)=(1-x^2)^{1/4}$, and retains 12 modal coefficients.

